# SYNTHETIC, not a real connector. Exercises contreforts/contreforts-workspace#83 (E2) item 3:
# once core ships its own canonical `core:CoreConcepts` scheme (concepts.ttl), the D2 lint's
# alignment-stub carve-out (src/lint/core_ns.rs) must stop accepting a connector that DEFINES a
# `core:`-namespaced `skos:Concept`/`skos:ConceptScheme` -- the exact shape that carve-out used
# to wave through deliberately, back when core had no scheme of its own to reference
# (contreforts-connector-forgejo#9's finding). A connector may still REFERENCE a core concept
# (as the object of `skos:exactMatch`/`closeMatch`/`inScheme`, see
# core-ns-references-concept-only.ttl-shaped assertions inside the real fixtures once they drop
# their own stubs) -- it may just no longer mint one itself.
#
# `core:test-defined-concept` is deliberately NOT one of the 15 real EntityKind terms, so this
# fixture cannot be confused with a legitimate use of core's real scheme -- the only thing wrong
# here is that a connector-authored file asserts `rdf:type skos:Concept` on a `core:` subject at
# all.
@prefix rdfs:         <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix sh:           <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix xsd:          <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix skos:         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix contreforts:  <https://contreforts.ds-labs.org/ontologies/declaration#> .
@prefix synth:        <https://contreforts.ds-labs.org/ontologies/synthetic-test#> .
@prefix core:         <https://contreforts.ds-labs.org/ontologies/core#> .

# The pre-E2 alignment-stub shape, verbatim -- previously the sanctioned carve-out, now the
# violation D2 must reject: a connector must not be the one defining this triple.
core:test-defined-concept a skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme core:CoreConcepts ;
    skos:prefLabel "Test defined concept"@en .

synth:SyntheticConnectorShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass synth:SyntheticConnector ;
    contreforts:category "test-only" ;
    sh:property [
        sh:path synth:label ;
        sh:name "Label" ;
        sh:datatype xsd:string ;
        sh:minCount 1 ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
    ] .
